      "id": 1,
      "text": "Florham Park became an official borough on March 9, 1899, carved out of Chatham Township.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Florham_Park%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name blends two Gilded Age estates: Florence and Hamilton Twombly’s Florham and a later mansion that now houses Brooklake Country Club.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        4,
        20,
        21
